  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1073,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 1089,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153412,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 221,
        "headingId": 1089,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> fibrosarcoma; neurofibrosarcoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T14:41:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1074,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 1090,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153413,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 221,
        "headingId": 1090,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T14:41:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1075,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 1091,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153414,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 221,
        "headingId": 1091,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours have been mostly documented in the uterine cervix and (less frequently) uterine corpus {35713627}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T14:41:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1076,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 1092,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153415,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 221,
        "headingId": 1092,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most patients present with vaginal bleeding or a cervical mass.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T14:41:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1077,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 1093,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153416,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 221,
        "headingId": 1093,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The incidence of the <em>NTRK</em>-rearranged spindle cell sarcoma is extremely low, and information on occurrence is provided by a limited number of case reports and series, especially for uncommon localizations. Although this tumour typically arises in the uterine cervix of young women, reported cases range in age from&nbsp;13 to 69&nbsp;years (mean: 31&nbsp;years) {21317712; 29553955; 34430691; 35713627} [[Moh M, Johnson CM, Geurts J, et al. Uterine Sarcoma with a Novel WWOX::NTRK2 Fusion in a Postmenopausal Woman with Li-Fraumeni&ndash;like Syndrome: A Case That Expands the Spectrum of NTRK-Rearranged Uterine Tumours. AJSP Rev Rep. 2021;26:304&ndash;306. DOI: 10.1097/PCR.0000000000000476]].</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T14:41:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1078,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 1094,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153417,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 221,
        "headingId": 1094,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T14:41:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1079,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 1095,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153418,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 221,
        "headingId": 1095,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Other than an association with <em>NTRK1&ndash;3</em> rearrangements, the pathogenesis of these neoplasms is unknown. <em>NTRK1</em> fusion partners include <em>LMNA, NUMA1, TPM3</em>, <em>TPR</em>, HAPSTR1 (<em>C16orf72</em><em>)</em>, and <em>IRF2BP2</em>, while <em>NTRK3</em> partners include <em>RBPMS, TFG, STRN3</em>, <em>SPECC1L</em><em>,</em> and <em>EML4 </em>{35713627; 38151535; 29553955; 31971278}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T14:41:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1086,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 1102,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153419,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 221,
        "headingId": 1102,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>NTRK</em>-rearranged spindle cell sarcomas are typically firm, slightly fleshy lesions centred in the cervical stroma and less frequently the myometrium. They range in size from 13&nbsp;to 230&nbsp;mm {34723848; 31107720; 35713627}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T14:41:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1080,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 1096,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153420,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 221,
        "headingId": 1096,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>NTRK</em>-rearranged spindle cell sarcoma consists of a proliferation of predominantly uniform spindle cells with mild to moderate and occasionally severe atypia and inconspicuous nucleoli. Scattered atypical symplastic-like cells may be present. The mitotic count is variable (&lt;&nbsp;1&nbsp;to 20&nbsp;mitoses/mm<sup>2</sup>). A staghorn vascular pattern, hyalinized vessels, nuclear pseudoinclusions, and necrosis may be present. Vascular invasion is uncommon. The spindle cells variably express S100, CD34, SMA, and cyclin&nbsp;D1. Pan-TRK expression is a sensitive, but not specific, marker for an underlying <em>NTRK1&ndash;3</em> rearrangement {37988282; 33290352}. Importantly, there is no expression of CD10, desmin, BCOR, ER, or PR {30877273; 21317712; 35713627}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T14:41:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1081,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 1097,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153421,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 221,
        "headingId": 1097,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Smears show a mixed pattern of sparse and dense tissue fragments of oval/spindle cells with eosinophilic amorphous material in the background {39670651}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T14:41:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1082,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 1098,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153422,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 221,
        "headingId": 1098,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Demonstration of <em>NTRK1&ndash;3</em> rearrangement is diagnostic.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T14:41:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1085,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 1101,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153423,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 221,
        "headingId": 1101,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> spindle cell sarcoma with <em>NTRK1&ndash;3</em> rearrangement.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable</em>: absence of CD10, desmin, ER, and PR expression.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T14:41:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1083,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 1099,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153424,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 221,
        "headingId": 1099,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>NTRK</em>-rearranged spindle cell sarcoma is staged as uterine sarcoma using FIGO, Union for International Cancer Control (UICC), and American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) systems.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T14:41:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1084,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 1100,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153425,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 221,
        "headingId": 1100,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The clinical course of <em>NTRK</em>-rearranged spindle cell sarcoma is variable, but at least some tumours are associated with metastasis and an aggressive clinical course. Data are limited, but tumours with lymphovascular invasion, necrosis, &gt;&nbsp;3.3&nbsp;mitoses/mm<sup>2</sup>, or <em>NTRK3 </em>fusion appear to be at higher risk of adverse outcomes {35713627}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T14:41:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]